@startuml Linkwise_Chat_Deployment
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Latin Modern Roman"
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #2A9D8F
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 22
skinparam ranksep 28
title UML deployment: illustrative intermittent global topology (proposed)
node "Station A / Americas" as A {
 artifact "Agent A + local MCP" as AA
 artifact "Message store + station\nruntime" as AS
}
node "Station R / Atlantic region" as R {
 artifact "Relay service + local policy" as RS
 artifact "Durable relay spool" as RQ
}
node "Station B / Europe" as B {
 artifact "Agent B + local MCP" as BA
 artifact "Message store + station\nruntime" as BS
}
node "Station C / Asia-Pacific" as C {
 artifact "Agent C + local MCP" as CA
 artifact "Message store + station\nruntime" as CS
}
A <--> B : direct HF contact when\neligible
A <--> R : scheduled HF window
R <--> B : later HF window
B <--> C : intermittent HF contact
A <..> C : possible future route; no\nreachability claim
note bottom of R
Each station includes its own radio, antenna,
identity and authority.
Lines represent candidate contacts, not always-on
network connections.
Geography is illustrative; route evidence must
establish eligibility.
end note
@enduml
